@startuml 09_sharding
title 9. Shared counter vs sharded counter
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
left to right direction

package "Shared: every thread increments ONE counter" {
  [Thread 0] as S0
  [Thread 1] as S1
  [Thread 7] as S7
  [x\n(one cache line)] as SX
  S0 --> SX
  S1 --> SX
  S7 --> SX
}

package "Sharded: each thread gets its OWN padded slot" {
  [Thread 0] as H0
  [Thread 1] as H1
  [Thread 7] as H7
  [slot 0\n(own line)] as HS0
  [slot 1\n(own line)] as HS1
  [slot 7\n(own line)] as HS7
  [reader: sum all slots\nwhen you need the total] as R
  H0 --> HS0
  H1 --> HS1
  H7 --> HS7
  HS0 --> R
  HS1 --> R
  HS7 --> R
}

footer Shared: total throughput falls as threads grow. Sharded: no line is contended, so it scales (7.6x on 8 cores in Experiment 5).
@enduml
